# A composed layer's demand, nameplate and draw each equal the sum of the converted parts, less what
# the composer eliminated against that quantity. One row per fusion that owes the equality in at
# least one quantity, `violates` where any owed quantity disagrees.
#
#     x_composed = F Φ x_parts − e
#
# The conformance rule for the headline equation
#   composition/fused.sqlc computes the sum, the filed figure and an `agrees` verdict;
#   matrices.sqlc, a psql tour, prints it, and examples/matrices/main.rs recomputes the product
#   in Rust. A verdict that only a tour prints and an example asserts is a verdict
#   reports/violations.sqlc and reports/coverage.sqlc cannot see, which is what a row on the
#   roster buys.
#
# The population is already correct
#   It must not be widened. composition/fused.sqlc inner joins composition/owed_equality.sqlc, so
#   a quantity suspended on any ground is absent here rather than counted as a pass. Adding the
#   suspended rows would report a document that declined to claim the equality as one that
#   satisfied it, which is the exact defect asrt:StatedEliminations was added to prevent.
#
# Every quantity, one verdict per fusion
#   composition/fused.sqlc is one row per (fusion, quantity). The rule's subject is the layer, as
#   checks/roster.sqlc declares, so the quantities fold into one verdict with `bool_or` and the
#   detail names each. Proof: `src/proofs/README.md`, entry `fusion_sum`.
#
# Two documents, so no grammar can state it
#   The parts are in one filing and the composed figure is in another; XSD 1.0 cannot follow the
#   reference, let alone add up what is on the other end.
-- asrt:Fusion/asrt:Part summed against the composed layer's demand, nameplate and draw, via composition/fused.sqlc.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT f.composition AS filing, f.composed_layer AS layer,
           bool_or(NOT f.agrees) AS violates,
           string_agg(format('%s: parts less eliminations give [%s, %s, %s]; the filing states [%s, %s, %s]',
                             f.quantity, f.computed_low, f.computed_mode, f.computed_high,
                             f.filed_low, f.filed_mode, f.filed_high),
                      '; ' ORDER BY f.quantity) AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(composition/fused.sqlc)
    ) f
    GROUP BY f.composition, f.composed_layer
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'fusion_sum_disagrees'
